#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""One-file builder for Bank_Peer_Monitor.

Plain ASCII (the code rides inside as base64), so it survives corporate
email and DLP intact. Run it on the target machine and it BUILDS the
workbook locally -- nothing binary is ever transmitted.

USAGE (PowerShell):
    python -m pip install pandas openpyxl
    python build_fdic_monitor.py

It writes into the current folder:
    Bank_Peer_Monitor.xlsm           (macro embedded, demo-populated)
    Bank_Peer_Monitor_fallback.xlsx  (no VBA; if Excel rejects the .xlsm, open this,
                      paste macro.bas via Alt+F11, save as .xlsm)
    runner.py, macro.bas, requirements.txt

Refresh later, with the workbook CLOSED:
    python runner.py --workbook ".\\Bank_Peer_Monitor.xlsm" --demo
    python runner.py --workbook ".\\Bank_Peer_Monitor.xlsm"           # LIVE -- the FDIC API is KEYLESS
    python runner.py --lookup "KeyBank"                            # find a CERT
    python runner.py --workbook ".\\Bank_Peer_Monitor.xlsm" --tieout 628  # verify a value
    Peers live in the _config [PEERS] table: edit a row and re-run, no rebuild.
"""
